{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Come now, let me take you.</b> He said <b>na</b> — meaning: now that what was, was, and whatever he had to bless he has already blessed them. And the reason he was still waiting for something is that he saw two times that HaShem desired blessing for Israel; it appears he thought it possible that the corner where Balaam stood one time and two times were [occupied by] righteous men, whereas now that he directed his face toward the entire people, presumably there would be among them one unfit group, and he thought perhaps he would find an opening to curse from there. And this is what he said: <b>perhaps it will be favorable</b>, etc. And he said <b>and build for me</b> rather than saying 'to build it' — by this he intended that there is no need for it to be favorable in the eyes of HaShem to build it, but rather that it be favorable in the eyes of HaShem not to prevent you, and then you will receive it from there."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:13:34.821010867Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}